:: Hallway #1 [nobr] {"position":"500,300","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <div class="speaker">Narrator</div>
    <<ctp "hallway">>
	    The wrong button. A pressure check begins. Then — the door opens. Not from your side.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    "Evidently, the goods don't need to pass many regulation checks to end up here. Don't worry, everything is still fine, but you just made things less adaptively convenient for yourself."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    "The pressure check is harmless. Just takes a moment longer."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    "Alright, well.. Things would have been easier if you met these things outside of this pod on your own terms, but I can assure you that they will do you no harm regardless thankfully. The door will open shortly. Not from your side."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    "When it does, you're going to see something in the corridor that will look alarming. Don't make sudden or unprovoked moves. You will just stay in there now and meet your observers who should know enough about you to just simply release you from this on their own accord."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Try talking to the alien|Exeption #1]]
            [[Move past|Hallway #2]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Hallway #2 [nobr] {"position":"800,300","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "hallway2">>
	    You move past the alien. It doesn't turn around. It doesn't need to — you can feel it tracking your presence without looking, the way something might register a shift in air pressure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    "Don't mind me, just passing through."
    <<ctpNext>>
	    A pause.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    "I can't believe that worked."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue down the hall|Observation Deck]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Intro Cinematic [nobr intro] {"position":"200,500","size":"100,100"}
<<audio awakening play>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "Intro">>
	    In 2071, we stopped feeling alone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      Unannounced and unprovokedly intrusive, or so it would seem. A structure several times bigger than the international space station appeared low in orbit, orbitally locking around the pacific ocean. Several small communities reported a strange unidentified flying object in the night sky, occassionally blowing up on social media and recieving various criticisms over their authenticity. The numerous governments and high standing organisations wasted no time however, containment of the exposure was in full force. The great war that happened a decade prior saw many people draw in the realisation that there might actually be some merit to numerous conspiracies around the elites hoarding the world’s wealth. The world wasn’t ready for a revelation as big as that was, so the information was classified.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      The following years weren’t so kind for the existing institutions who have just started trying to survive, the knowledge of an alternate lifeform, worse yet the supposedly enemy governments somehow organising surprisingly well in hiding the fact could have been devastating for the public trust and cooperation. 
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      By 2079 practically everyone knew. Undoubtedly.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      What followed wasn't first contact. It was the first of the invisible collapse. People started questioning the current local orders, the very environment they lived in, the people they thought they held close, the distant new force in the sky. 
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      The global econimic crisis of the upcoming decade portruded the sentiment even further, the sentiment that never got a call back, at least not from the right people. The fringe groups, all with their own idelogies offered solutions and promises that others wouldn’t, the groups people were previously skeptical of, all started recieving more attention from all angles. 
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      Over the next 20 years, seventeen governments fell. The ones that didn't fell, later, or were absorbed into something that called itself an order but functioned more like a pressure system, holding everything down so nothing could rise. A strong autoractic “federation” which represents the global order and the interests of all humans. 
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      In the huge gaps it left behind, other things grew. As they always do, but never before on this big of a scale. 
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      Criminal networks. Whole shadow governments. Organisations that don't have names you'd recognise but have reach you'd find impressive. Some of them made contact with the visitors. Not diplomatically quite as diplomatically as commercially.
  It turns out the visitors were curious about us. Not enough to fully intrude, but enough for them to have stuck around for decades since.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      The year is 2137. The diplomatic, albeit, not entirely documented relations between these unearthly visitors and the human collective have taken a.. turn that isn’t entirely unexpected. Seeing the results and potential prospects of these trades, many groups took to trading various artifacts and trinkets from them, usually in exchange for some mundane  items and biological samples.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      These samples unbeknownst to a majority of the people don’t exactly exclude.. other humans.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      Some people were unfortunately, against their own will, caught up in the newly present mercantile system that runs outside of the usual framework, and found that out the hard way.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      You are about to be one of them.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
      <div class="choice">[[Wake up|Awakening]]</div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



